.claude/plans/PLAN-179/rail-round-6/VERDICT.txt:7:  When `CEO_STATUSLINE_SIDECAR` points the statusline writer at a custom file, the normal PreCompact payload has no inline context accounting and this fallback still reads `<audit-dir>/state/statusline-snapshot.json`. `statusline-ceo.py:_sidecar_path()` writes to the override instead, so this function returns `None` and silently skips pressure telemetry; it should resolve the same override and fallback path as the writer.
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/rail-round-8/VERDICT.txt:9:  When hook `cwd` differs from the workspace root, such as after `CwdChanged` into a subdirectory, this rejects a valid sidecar because `statusline-ceo.py` stores `workspace.project_dir`, not the hook's current directory. Since production PreCompact inputs lack inline context accounting, the fallback then returns `None` and the pressure event remains silent. Compare the sidecar identity with the actual project root instead.
