    63	## How this template is actually used
    64	
    65	> **Verdict (PLAN-179 W3 / US10, recorded 2026-08-18).** This template is
    66	> **not** wired to anything automatically, and — inside Claude Code — it
    67	> **cannot be**. It is fed by a human, on one route only. The two candidate
    68	> routes were evaluated against what this repository can actually verify
    69	> locally; the evidence for each is named below. Do not read this section as
    70	> a promise of wiring: it is the honest boundary.
    71	
    72	### Route (a) — `/compact <instructions>` in the CLI · **USABLE, MANUAL ONLY**
    73	
    74	Typing `/compact` followed by instruction text hands that text to the
    75	harness's summarizer. Local evidence that the harness carries such a field:
    76	the pinned hook schema `.claude/data/hook-schema-2.1.220.json` declares
    77	
    78	    "PreCompact": { "trigger": "enum[manual,auto]",
    79	                    "custom_instructions": "string|null" }
    80	
    81	so a manual compaction genuinely transports operator-authored instructions.
    82	
    83	Two consequences follow from the SAME schema file, and both are load-bearing:
    84	
    85	1. **No hook can supply this template.** The schema's `_absent_arms_note`
    86	   lists `PreCompact` among the events with **no `hookSpecificOutput` arm** —
    87	   there is no `additionalContext`, and no field a hook may return to SET
    88	   `custom_instructions`. A `PreCompact` hook may observe the compaction, and
    89	   may BLOCK it (exit 2), but it cannot author the instruction. Automation of
    90	   this route is therefore not available; the operator pastes the template.
    91	2. **Auto-compaction gets nothing.** On `trigger = auto`,
    92	   `custom_instructions` is `null` — nobody typed anything. The auto path is
    93	   the DOMINANT path for long sessions (the exact finding recorded against
    94	   ADR-153), so this template covers the case that happens least often.
    95	
    96	### Route (b) — the API `instructions` parameter · **ADOPTER-ONLY, UNVERIFIED HERE**
    97	
    98	The server-side compaction tool takes an `instructions` string that replaces
    99	the default summarization prompt. Inside this repository that route is
   100	**documented but not exercised**: the only local description lives in
   101	`.claude/plans/PLAN-179/research-S309.md §1.1` (a research note citing the
   102	vendor docs — external content, recorded as DATA), and a repo-wide grep for
   103	the tool identifier and for `context_management` finds **no caller** — only
   104	plan and research prose. This framework installs into a Claude Code harness;
   105	it does not own an API request loop, so it cannot exercise route (b) at all.
   106	
   107	Route (b) is real for an **adopter** who owns their own API loop. For them,
   108	rendering this template into `instructions` is the wiring. For this
   109	repository, treat it as unverified-locally: mark any claim about it
   110	`(unverified)` until a probe demonstrates it end-to-end.
   111	
   112	### THE SHARP EDGE — `instructions` REPLACES, it does not append
   113	
   114	On route (b) the `instructions` string **substitutes the default
   115	summarization prompt in its entirety**. Nothing is merged and nothing warns
   116	you. Any recall the default prompt would have produced, and that this
   117	template does not explicitly ask for, is **silently lost** — the summary
   118	looks complete and is not. The same hazard applies in spirit to route (a):
   119	whatever you type steers the summarizer away from its default behaviour.
   120	
   121	Therefore:
   122	
   123	- Send the template **whole**. Trimming a section for brevity is deleting a
   124	  recall requirement, not saving tokens.
   125	- When you add a domain section, **add** it — never replace one of the nine.
   126	- A section with nothing to report is emitted as the literal `(none)`. That
   127	  is what distinguishes "nothing here" from "the instruction did not ask".
   128	- After a compaction driven by this template, spot-check that all nine
   129	  headers came back. A missing header is evidence of instruction loss, not
   130	  of an empty session.
   131	
   132	### Status of the automatic route
   133	
   134	**BLOCKED ON A PROBE.** No automatic route exists today, and route (a) is
   135	structurally closed to automation for the reason given above. Any future
   136	claim that this template feeds compaction automatically must cite a probe
   137	that (i) emits a unique canary through the chosen channel and (ii) FAILS when
   138	the canary is withheld — a positive control. Until such a probe exists, the
   139	honest description of this file is: *a manual instruction the operator
   140	pastes, plus a shape contract the nine sections below define.*
