    11	dispatch loop, and only the subset the frozen template uses (11 steps, pinned
    12	by .claude/scripts/tests/test_validate_template_frozen_subset.py):
    13	
    14	  * steps run IN ORDER, each in its own ``bash --noprofile --norc -eo
    15	    pipefail <script>`` (the runner's default shell for ``run:`` on Linux
    16	    runners), cwd = the workspace, the job stops at the FIRST failing step;
    17	  * ``uses:`` steps are runner-provided (checkout, setup-*) and are SKIPPED
    18	    BY NAME on stdout — never silently;
    19	  * the job-level ``if:`` must be the repository-variable kill switch the
    20	    frozen template uses (``vars.X != '1'``) — reported and treated as
    21	    "variable unset" (the job runs), which is what a fresh adopter
    22	    repository has; any other expression is a parse failure;
    23	  * the JOB-LEVEL keys are whitelisted (name, runs-on, if, timeout-minutes,
    24	    steps) and ``runs-on`` must be an ubuntu runner: a job that gains
    25	    ``env:``/``container:``/``strategy:``/``defaults:`` or moves off ubuntu
    26	    fails the parse instead of executing under silently different local
    27	    semantics (rail r2, S337), and the WORKFLOW-LEVEL keys are whitelisted
    28	    too — name, on, concurrency, permissions, jobs; a top-level ``env:`` or
    29	    ``defaults:`` is a parse failure (rail r3, S337);
    30	  * the job-level ``timeout-minutes`` is HONOURED as a wall-clock deadline
    31	    over the whole job (rail r1, S337): a step still running when it expires
    32	    is killed and the job FAILS, exactly as the hosted runner cancels it —
    33	    otherwise a step that takes 20 minutes would pass here and be cancelled
    34	    on GitHub. Default when absent: 360 minutes (the hosted default);
    35	  * runner environment: ``GITHUB_WORKSPACE`` = the workspace, ``RUNNER_TEMP``
    36	    = a fresh temp dir, ``CI`` / ``GITHUB_ACTIONS`` = ``true``, ``RUNNER_OS``
    37	    per platform.
    38	
    39	Anything OUTSIDE that subset — a step-level ``if:``, ``shell:``,
    40	``working-directory:``, ``env:``, ``continue-on-error:``, a step-level
    41	``timeout-minutes:``, a second job, a step with neither ``uses:`` nor
    42	``run:`` — is a parse failure (exit 2), not a guess. A template that outgrows
    43	this parser must surface as a failure, never as a vacuous pass (CLAUDE.md §5:
    44	"instrumento verde cuja PERGUNTA envelheceu").
    45	
    46	stdlib only: PyYAML is a third-party module and the framework runtime is
    47	stdlib-only (CLAUDE.md §4), so the parser reads the frozen template's YAML
    48	shape (block-scalar ``run: |``, single-line ``run:``, ``uses:``) directly.
    49	
    50	Usage:
    51	    run-activated-workflow.py <workspace> <workflow-relpath> [--list]
    52	
    53	Exit codes:
    54	    0  every ``run:`` step passed (and at least one ran)
    55	    1  a ``run:`` step failed, or the job deadline expired (name printed)
    56	    2  usage / parse failure (unsupported shape, no job, no run step)
    57	"""
    58	from __future__ import annotations
    59	
    60	import os
    61	import platform
    62	import re
    63	import subprocess
    64	import sys
    65	import tempfile
    66	import time
    67	from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple
    68	
    69	# Keys a step may carry, and what each one means to this runner.
    70	_STEP_KEYS_SUPPORTED = ("name", "uses", "run", "with")
    71	# Job-level keys this runner models. Anything else (env:, defaults:,
    72	# container:, strategy:, services:, permissions: …) changes execution
    73	# semantics the local dispatch loop does not reproduce — parse failure, not a
    74	# silent local approximation (rail r2, S337).
    75	_JOB_KEYS_SUPPORTED = ("name", "runs-on", "if", "timeout-minutes", "steps")
    76	# Workflow-level keys this runner models. `on:` and `concurrency:` govern WHEN
    77	# the hosted job runs (trigger plumbing — execution-neutral here); a top-level
    78	# `permissions:` only RESTRICTS the token. `env:` or `defaults:` would change
    79	# the environment/shell semantics of every step — parse failure (rail r3).
    80	_TOP_KEYS_SUPPORTED = ("name", "on", "concurrency", "permissions", "jobs")
    81	# The one job-level `if:` shape the frozen template uses: a repository-variable
    82	# kill switch. Any other expression would need the Actions expression engine.
    83	_JOB_IF_SHAPE = re.compile(r"vars\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\s*!=\s*'1'")
    84	_STEP_KEYS_UNSUPPORTED = (
    85	    "if", "shell", "working-directory", "env", "continue-on-error",
    86	    "timeout-minutes", "id",
    87	)
    88	_DEFAULT_JOB_TIMEOUT_MIN = 360  # the hosted runner's default
    89	
    90	
    91	class ParseError(Exception):
    92	    pass
    93	
    94	
    95	def _indent(line: str) -> int:
    96	    return len(line) - len(line.lstrip(" "))
    97	
    98	
    99	def _is_blank_or_comment(line: str) -> bool:
   100	    s = line.strip()
   101	    return not s or s.startswith("#")
   102	
   103	
   104	def _find_key_line(lines: List[str], key: str, indent: int, start: int, stop: int) -> Optional[int]:
   105	    """Index of the first line in [start, stop) that is ``key:`` at exactly ``indent``."""
   106	    pat = re.compile(r"^ {%d}%s:(\s|$)" % (indent, re.escape(key)))
   107	    for i in range(start, stop):
   108	        if pat.match(lines[i]):
   109	            return i
   110	    return None
   111	
   112	
   113	def _block_end(lines: List[str], start: int, indent: int) -> int:
   114	    """First index after ``start`` whose content is at indent <= ``indent``
   115	    (blank/comment lines never end a block)."""
   116	    i = start + 1
   117	    while i < len(lines):
   118	        if not _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]) and _indent(lines[i]) <= indent:
   119	            return i
   120	        i += 1
   121	    return len(lines)
   122	
   123	
   124	def _scalar_value(lines: List[str], idx: int, key_indent: int) -> Tuple[str, int]:
   125	    """Value of the scalar at ``lines[idx]`` (``key: value`` or ``key: |``
   126	    block). Returns (value, index_after)."""
   127	    line = lines[idx]
   128	    after = line.split(":", 1)[1]
   129	    stripped = after.strip()
   130	    end = _block_end(lines, idx, key_indent)
   131	    if stripped in ("|", "|-", "|+", ">", ">-"):
   132	        if stripped.startswith(">"):
   133	            # Folded scalars are not used by the frozen template; refuse
   134	            # rather than approximate the folding rules.
   135	            raise ParseError("folded scalar (>) at line %d is not supported" % (idx + 1))
   136	        body = lines[idx + 1:end]
   137	        content = [l for l in body if l.strip()]
   138	        if not content:
   139	            raise ParseError("empty block scalar at line %d" % (idx + 1))
   140	        base = min(_indent(l) for l in content)
   141	        out = []
   142	        for l in body:
   143	            out.append(l[base:] if len(l) >= base else "")
   144	        return "\n".join(out).rstrip("\n") + "\n", end
   145	    if stripped == "":
   146	        raise ParseError("key at line %d has no value" % (idx + 1))
   147	    if stripped[0] in "\"'" and stripped[-1] == stripped[0] and len(stripped) >= 2:
   148	        stripped = stripped[1:-1]
   149	    return stripped + "\n", idx + 1
   150	
   151	
   152	def _job_scalar(lines: List[str], key: str, indent: int, start: int, stop: int) -> Optional[str]:
   153	    idx = _find_key_line(lines, key, indent, start, stop)
   154	    if idx is None:
   155	        return None
   156	    return lines[idx].split(":", 1)[1].strip()
   157	
   158	
   159	def parse_workflow(text: str) -> Dict[str, object]:
   160	    lines = text.splitlines()
   161	    n = len(lines)
   162	
   163	    # rail r3 (S337): whitelist the WORKFLOW-LEVEL keys before anything else —
   164	    # a top-level env:/defaults: changes every step, and skipping straight to
   165	    # jobs: would execute under silently different semantics.
   166	    for i in range(0, n):
   167	        if _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]) or _indent(lines[i]) != 0:
   168	            continue
   169	        m = re.match(r"^([A-Za-z-]+):", lines[i])
   170	        if not m:
   171	            raise ParseError("unexpected top-level line at %d: %r" % (i + 1, lines[i]))
   172	        if m.group(1) not in _TOP_KEYS_SUPPORTED:
   173	            raise ParseError("workflow uses top-level `%s:` (line %d), which this runner does not model" % (
   174	                m.group(1), i + 1))
   175	
   176	    jobs_idx = _find_key_line(lines, "jobs", 0, 0, n)
   177	    if jobs_idx is None:
   178	        raise ParseError("no top-level `jobs:` key")
   179	    jobs_end = _block_end(lines, jobs_idx, 0)
   180	
   181	    # Job ids: first-level children of jobs:.
   182	    job_ids: List[Tuple[int, str]] = []
   183	    job_indent = None
   184	    for i in range(jobs_idx + 1, jobs_end):
   185	        if _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]):
   186	            continue
   187	        ind = _indent(lines[i])
   188	        if job_indent is None:
   189	            job_indent = ind
   190	        if ind == job_indent:
   191	            m = re.match(r"^ *([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*):\s*$", lines[i])
   192	            if not m:
   193	                raise ParseError("unexpected line under jobs: at %d: %r" % (i + 1, lines[i]))
   194	            job_ids.append((i, m.group(1)))
   195	    if len(job_ids) != 1:
   196	        raise ParseError("expected exactly one job, found %d (%s)" % (
   197	            len(job_ids), ", ".join(j for _, j in job_ids)))
   198	    job_idx, job_id = job_ids[0]
   199	    assert job_indent is not None
   200	    job_end = _block_end(lines, job_idx, job_indent)
   201	    body_indent = job_indent + 2
   202	
   203	    # rail r2 (S337): whitelist the JOB-LEVEL keys before reading any of them —
   204	    # a job that gains env:/container:/strategy:/defaults: must fail the parse,
   205	    # never execute under a silently different local environment.
   206	    for i in range(job_idx + 1, job_end):
   207	        if _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]) or _indent(lines[i]) != body_indent:
   208	            continue
   209	        m = re.match(r"^ *([A-Za-z-]+):", lines[i])
   210	        if not m:
   211	            raise ParseError("unexpected line in job body at %d: %r" % (i + 1, lines[i]))
   212	        if m.group(1) not in _JOB_KEYS_SUPPORTED:
   213	            raise ParseError("job %r uses `%s:` (line %d), which this runner does not model" % (
   214	                job_id, m.group(1), i + 1))
   215	
   216	    runs_on = _job_scalar(lines, "runs-on", body_indent, job_idx + 1, job_end)
   217	    if runs_on is None or not runs_on.startswith("ubuntu-"):
   218	        raise ParseError("job %r runs-on %r — this local runner only models ubuntu runners" % (
   219	            job_id, runs_on))
   220	
   221	    job_if = _job_scalar(lines, "if", body_indent, job_idx + 1, job_end)
   222	    if job_if is not None:
   223	        stripped_if = job_if.strip()
   224	        if stripped_if.startswith("${{") and stripped_if.endswith("}}"):
   225	            stripped_if = stripped_if[3:-2].strip()
   226	        if not _JOB_IF_SHAPE.fullmatch(stripped_if):
   227	            raise ParseError("job %r has an if: expression this runner does not model: %r" % (
   228	                job_id, job_if))
   229	
   230	    timeout_raw = _job_scalar(lines, "timeout-minutes", body_indent, job_idx + 1, job_end)
   231	    if timeout_raw is None:
   232	        job_timeout_min = _DEFAULT_JOB_TIMEOUT_MIN
   233	    else:
   234	        if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", timeout_raw) or int(timeout_raw) <= 0:
   235	            raise ParseError("job %r has a non-integer timeout-minutes: %r" % (job_id, timeout_raw))
   236	        job_timeout_min = int(timeout_raw)
   237	
   238	    steps_idx = _find_key_line(lines, "steps", body_indent, job_idx + 1, job_end)
   239	    if steps_idx is None:
   240	        raise ParseError("job %r has no steps:" % job_id)
   241	    steps_end = _block_end(lines, steps_idx, body_indent)
   242	
   243	    # Step items: `- name:` lines at the item indent (first item defines it).
   244	    item_indent = None
   245	    item_starts: List[int] = []
   246	    for i in range(steps_idx + 1, steps_end):
   247	        if _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]):
   248	            continue
   249	        ind = _indent(lines[i])
   250	        if item_indent is None:
   251	            item_indent = ind
   252	        if ind == item_indent:
   253	            if not re.match(r"^ *- name:\s*\S", lines[i]):
   254	                raise ParseError("step item at line %d does not start with `- name:`: %r" % (i + 1, lines[i]))
   255	            item_starts.append(i)
   256	        elif ind < item_indent:
   257	            raise ParseError("dedent inside steps at line %d" % (i + 1))
   258	    if not item_starts:
   259	        raise ParseError("job %r has an empty steps: list" % job_id)
   260	    assert item_indent is not None
   261	    key_indent = item_indent + 2
   262	
   263	    steps: List[Dict[str, object]] = []
   264	    for k, s in enumerate(item_starts):
   265	        e = item_starts[k + 1] if k + 1 < len(item_starts) else steps_end
   266	        name = lines[s].split(":", 1)[1].strip()
   267	        if name[:1] in "\"'" and name[-1:] == name[:1] and len(name) >= 2:
   268	            name = name[1:-1]
   269	        keys: Dict[str, int] = {}
   270	        i = s + 1
   271	        while i < e:
   272	            if _is_blank_or_comment(lines[i]):
   273	                i += 1
   274	                continue
   275	            if _indent(lines[i]) != key_indent:
   276	                raise ParseError("unexpected indentation inside step %r at line %d: %r" % (name, i + 1, lines[i]))
   277	            m = re.match(r"^ *([A-Za-z_-]+):", lines[i])
   278	            if not m:
   279	                raise ParseError("unexpected line inside step %r at line %d: %r" % (name, i + 1, lines[i]))
   280	            key = m.group(1)
   281	            if key in _STEP_KEYS_UNSUPPORTED:
   282	                raise ParseError("step %r uses `%s:` (line %d), which this runner does not model" % (name, key, i + 1))
   283	            if key not in _STEP_KEYS_SUPPORTED:
   284	                raise ParseError("step %r uses unknown key `%s:` (line %d)" % (name, key, i + 1))
   285	            if key in keys:
   286	                raise ParseError("step %r repeats key `%s:` (line %d)" % (name, key, i + 1))
   287	            keys[key] = i
   288	            i = _block_end(lines, i, key_indent)
   289	        has_uses = "uses" in keys
   290	        has_run = "run" in keys
   291	        if has_uses == has_run:
   292	            raise ParseError("step %r must have exactly one of uses:/run:" % name)
   293	        if "with" in keys and not has_uses:
   294	            raise ParseError("step %r has with: without uses:" % name)
   295	        if has_uses:
   296	            uses, _ = _scalar_value(lines, keys["uses"], key_indent)
   297	            steps.append({"name": name, "kind": "uses", "uses": uses.strip()})
   298	        else:
   299	            script, _ = _scalar_value(lines, keys["run"], key_indent)
   300	            steps.append({"name": name, "kind": "run", "script": script})
   301	
   302	    return {"job_id": job_id, "job_if": job_if, "timeout_min": job_timeout_min, "steps": steps}
   303	
   304	
   305	def _runner_env(workspace: str, runner_temp: str) -> Dict[str, str]:
   306	    env = dict(os.environ)
   307	    env.update({
   308	        "GITHUB_WORKSPACE": workspace,
   309	        "RUNNER_TEMP": runner_temp,
   310	        "RUNNER_TOOL_CACHE": runner_temp,
   311	        "CI": "true",
   312	        "GITHUB_ACTIONS": "true",
   313	        "RUNNER_OS": {"Linux": "Linux", "Darwin": "macOS", "Windows": "Windows"}.get(
   314	            platform.system(), platform.system()),
   315	    })
   316	    return env
   317	
   318	
   319	def main(argv: List[str]) -> int:
   320	    args = [a for a in argv[1:] if not a.startswith("--")]
   321	    flags = {a for a in argv[1:] if a.startswith("--")}
   322	    if len(args) != 2 or flags - {"--list"}:
   323	        sys.stderr.write(__doc__.split("Usage:", 1)[1].split("Exit codes:", 1)[0])
   324	        return 2
   325	    workspace = os.path.realpath(args[0])
   326	    wf_rel = args[1]
   327	    wf_path = os.path.join(workspace, wf_rel)
   328	    if not os.path.isdir(workspace):
   329	        sys.stderr.write("run-activated-workflow: workspace is not a directory: %s\n" % workspace)
   330	        return 2
   331	    if wf_rel.endswith(".template"):
   332	        sys.stderr.write("run-activated-workflow: refusing a .template — activate it first (the adopter's mv)\n")
   333	        return 2
   334	    if not os.path.isfile(wf_path):
   335	        sys.stderr.write("run-activated-workflow: workflow not found: %s\n" % wf_path)
   336	        return 2
   337	
   338	    try:
   339	        with open(wf_path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
   340	            wf = parse_workflow(fh.read())
   341	    except ParseError as exc:
   342	        sys.stderr.write("run-activated-workflow: PARSE FAILURE in %s: %s\n" % (wf_rel, exc))
   343	        return 2
   344	
   345	    steps = wf["steps"]  # type: ignore[assignment]
   346	    assert isinstance(steps, list)
   347	    timeout_min = int(wf["timeout_min"])  # type: ignore[arg-type]
   348	    run_steps = [s for s in steps if s["kind"] == "run"]
   349	    print("==> activated workflow: %s (job %r, %d steps: %d run, %d uses; timeout-minutes %d)" % (
   350	        wf_rel, wf["job_id"], len(steps), len(run_steps), len(steps) - len(run_steps), timeout_min))
   351	    if wf["job_if"]:
   352	        print("    job-level if: %s — treated as unset repository variable (job runs)" % wf["job_if"])
   353	    if not run_steps:
   354	        sys.stderr.write("run-activated-workflow: no run: step — nothing would execute (refusing a vacuous pass)\n")
   355	        return 2
   356	
   357	    if "--list" in flags:
   358	        for i, s in enumerate(steps, 1):
   359	            if s["kind"] == "uses":
   360	                print("  %2d. [uses] %s  (%s)" % (i, s["name"], s["uses"]))
     1	"""PLAN-183 W2 — Ramo B: subconjunto congelado do validate.yml.template.
     2	
     3	O vínculo template↔vivo escolhido na abertura da wave (S334) é o Ramo B
     4	do Check: em vez de um gate de drift contra o validate.yml vivo (71
     5	steps, superfície de cerimônia própria), o template entregue ao adopter
     6	é DECLARADO aqui como subconjunto mínimo congelado — cada step nomeado —
     7	e este teste falha se o template divergir da declaração em qualquer
     8	direção: step a mais, a menos, fora de ordem, pin perdido, ou o retorno
     9	de um dos três steps removidos por `4f750f0` (verde-vácuo / falso-verde
    10	no adopter, `PLAN-183/resposta-ao-campo.md` §A2).
    11	
    12	Stdlib-only por contrato (CLAUDE.md §4): o parse é textual, sem PyYAML.
    13	"""
    14	from __future__ import annotations
    15	
    16	import re
    17	import sys
    18	import unittest
