.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:13:  Minimal fix: terminate help extraction at the Bash sentinel, as `doctor.sh` now does, and rename the option description to “backup HMAC sidecar.”
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:16:  Concrete failure: condition 5 says byte-identical ownership has an effect only during explicit uninstall. Once recorded as framework-owned, `doctor.sh` also classifies later edits as adopter drift and can back up and overwrite them under explicit `--repair` confirmation.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r2/verdict-rc1-3.txt:17:  Minimal fix: describe both consequences: uninstall deletion and doctor verification/confirmed restoration.
