.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r13/verdict-rc1-1.txt:8:  Cenário concreto: o template do gate mudou de `83ff8e9…` para `78e32dc…`, corrigindo o log global que permitia reutilizar uma aprovação entre repositórios ([pre-push-review-gate.sh:144](<WT>/templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:144)). O helper classifica o gate pristine da v1.3.0 como colisão simplesmente porque difere, retorna 2 sob o `--on-conflict=refuse` padrão, e o upgrader ignora o retorno, grava `upgrade_succeeded:true` e imprime “Upgrade complete”. Assim o defeito cross-project permanece.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r13/verdict-rc1-1.txt:16:  Cenário concreto: seguindo o workaround `--on-conflict backup`, os três outputs Grok idênticos não entram em `_GROK_MANIFEST_EMITS`; o manifesto é então sobrescrito somente com o gate alterado e não carrega registros anteriores. Um uninstall posterior deixa `AGENTS.md` e os exemplos `.grok/` para trás e perde referências a backups antigos.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r13/PROVENANCE-rc1.md:12:- parte 3 (doctor.sh + uninstall.sh + templates/** entregues): (VERDICT ambiguo:  linhas - inspecionar transcript; rc=99) [codex rc=99]
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r2/verdict-rc1-2.txt:5:   **Concrete failure:** Condition 5 says byte-equality ownership affects only an explicit uninstall. That is false for `CODEOWNERS`. An adopter-authored file matching the rendered output is skipped but added to the framework manifest. If the adopter later empties it intentionally to disable review routing, `_codeowners_provenance` treats that manifest row as proof of delivery and a subsequent install re-renders the file, silently re-enabling routing. The claimed file is equal to rendered output, not necessarily to the public template’s literal bytes.
