.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r8/verdict-rc1-3.txt:8:  Concrete failure: condition 50 says restore moves the live `.claude/` “before any check.” The diff now verifies an optional HMAC, lists the archive, requires a `.claude` member, and completes dry-run before that move. For example, `--dry-run --restore README.md` exits 4 during `tar tzf` and never moves `.claude`. The predictable, unconfined aside defect remains for a valid non-dry-run archive, but the proposed signed description is false.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r8/verdict-rc1-3.txt:9:  Minimal fix: state that the move occurs after existence/HMAC/archive-name validation and the dry-run boundary, but before extraction, then repin the envelope provenance.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-6.txt:17:   The compatibility branch preserves legacy HMAC sidecars under `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` and returns that directory at `:243`, but candidate writers unconditionally move their lock to the `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` parent in `audit_emit.py:2382` and `spool_writer.py:422`. During an in-session upgrade, an old v1.3 hook locks `LOG_DIR` while a new hook locks `LOG_PATH.parent`; both append to the same log and mutate the same legacy chain sidecars. This can fork the HMAC chain or lose the chain-length increment. Minimal fix: centralize the preservation decision so key, sidecars, and lock remain under one directory, or require a quiesced atomic migration before switching locks.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r8/verdict-rc1-2.txt:5:- **P1 — [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:218](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:218), [scripts/install.sh:2071](<WT>/scripts/install.sh:2071), [scripts/upgrade.sh:4803](<WT>/scripts/upgrade.sh:4803), [scripts/upgrade.sh:4848](<WT>/scripts/upgrade.sh:4848).** A condição 5 afirma que o “install/upgrade seguinte” re-renderiza um `CODEOWNERS` posteriormente esvaziado. Só o installer possui essa recuperação. No upgrader, o hash do arquivo vazio não coincide com baseline, geração atual ou histórica, portanto cai em `PRESERVED adopter-modified`. **Correção mínima:** trocar por “o re-run seguinte de `install.sh` re-renderiza”; manter `doctor --repair` e uninstall como efeitos separados e regenerar o hash/proveniência do envelope.
