.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-1.txt:5:- P1 — `scripts/upgrade.sh:4746` — Concrete failure: byte equality alone causes an existing file to be registered as framework-owned at line 4755. A v1.3.0 adopter-authored `.github/CODEOWNERS.template` identical to the shipped template—previously skipped and absent from the old manifest—is claimed by this upgrade; a later manifest-honoring uninstall deletes it. Minimal fix: treat an equal pre-existing file without a prior delivery record as `PRESERVED (unclaimed)` and do not register it.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:1:P1 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:364`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:370`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:373`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:376`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:2:A valid `--link` manifest record has the form `LINK  <relpath>  <target>`, but uninstall parses every record as `<sha>  <relpath>`. The resulting “relpath” contains both destination and target, so `_rel_unsafe` rejects it for containing a space. A repository installed with v1.3.0 `--link`, then upgraded to this candidate, cannot uninstall those deliveries: symlinks remain and the manifest is kept. The backup pass makes the same parsing error, so non-`.claude` link deliveries are also absent from the recovery archive. Minimal fix: parse LINK and hash records separately using the shared manifest grammar; unlink only when the current symlink target matches the recorded target, and add a v1.3 link-install → candidate-upgrade → uninstall/restore integration test.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:4:P1 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:436`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:454`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:5:The new security refusal path reports an “incomplete” uninstall but exits 0. Automation therefore records success after a traversal record, symlinked ancestor, or every valid LINK record described above was refused. This is fail-open at the process boundary and also contradicts the documented non-success exit behavior. Minimal fix: return nonzero whenever `unsafe_count > 0`; use the documented mismatch exit for non-forced SHA mismatches, and make tests assert failure status as well as log text.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:7:P1 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:89`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:369`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:403`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:10:P1 — `scripts/uninstall.sh:318`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:340`, `scripts/uninstall.sh:350`  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:11:The pre-uninstall archive and HMAC use predictable, second-resolution paths without destination confinement or exclusive creation. A pre-existing symlink or hard link named `.claude.backup-uninstall-<timestamp>.tar.gz`—or its `.hmac` sidecar—causes the write to follow or modify another inode, potentially outside the target. Minimal fix: create unpredictable files exclusively inside a physically validated target directory, refuse linked destinations, and atomically rename only after archive and HMAC generation succeed.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/verdict-rc1-3.txt:19:VERDICT: NO-GO — rc.1 should wait for the LINK/untrusted-manifest uninstall failures, backup destination escape, and validation-workflow fail-open and supply-chain defects to be fixed and covered by negative integration tests.
