.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r10/verdict-rc1-2.txt:7:- **P1 — `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:251`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1310`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1392`; afirmação contrária em `scripts/install.sh:3077`.** O manifesto do installer percorre recursivamente `.claude/hooks`, `.claude/scripts`, `.claude/commands` e diretórios de skills no **alvo**, não o conjunto realmente entregue. Assim, `.claude/hooks/acme_local.py`, nunca presente na fonte e nunca escrito pelo installer, recebe seu próprio hash como baseline framework-owned. Se permanecer inalterado, `uninstall.sh:616-622` o remove. As condições 5 e 64 cobrem igualdade com templates e colisões em caminhos novos, não arquivos autorais arbitrários dentro dessas árvores. **Correção mínima:** gerar o manifesto a partir de um ledger de entregas reais e continuidade validada; nunca expandir diretórios do alvo como prova de posse.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r15/verdict-rc1-4.txt:8:- Claim or overwrite adopter-authored files through byte equality, historical-template equality, new-path collisions, or unconditional dispatcher/agent delivery; later upgrades, doctor, or uninstall then treat them as framework-owned (5, 42, 48, 61, 64, 75).
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:2:scripts/uninstall.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:5:templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:8:templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/verdict-rc1-3.txt:1:- **P1 — [scripts/uninstall.sh:395](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:395), [scripts/uninstall.sh:427](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:427), [scripts/uninstall.sh:497](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:497), [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:660](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:660).** The new parser accepts every syntactically valid occurrence of a relpath; it never checks uniqueness. With `<old-sha>  docs/x` followed by `<current-sha>  docs/x`, the first record reports the adopter-modified file as preserved, but the second removes that same file without `--force` at line 531. The eventual exit 5 occurs after the deletion. The envelope is demonstrably false when condition 61 says this sanitizer already refuses duplicated manifests. It also does not refuse a symlinked manifest: the `-f` check at [line 350](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:350) follows it. Minimal fix: require a regular, non-symlink manifest and reject every occurrence of an ambiguous relpath before backup or removal, using doctor’s two-pass duplicate handling; add a conflicting-duplicate test proving no file is removed. Correct condition 61 accordingly.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/verdict-rc1-3.txt:9:VERDICT: NO-GO — Condition 61 falsely credits the uninstaller with rejecting duplicate and symlinked manifests, leaving an undeclared P1 deletion path without `--force`.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r10/NOTE.md:5:- Parte 3: VERDICT: NO-GO — Condition 69’s leaf-only manifest cure misses a P1 ancestor-symlink escape affecting both doctor and uninstall.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:2:scripts/uninstall.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:5:templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/paths-rc1-3.manifest.txt:8:templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:3:- P1 — [scripts/uninstall.sh:380](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:380), [scripts/uninstall.sh:399](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:399), [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:112](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:112). The new “total parser” is not total on the supported Bash 3.2 floor. `read -r` discards a NUL and the remainder of that record before the new `grep '[[:cntrl:]]'` check sees it. A manifest record `<valid-sha>  docs/file<NUL>garbage` is therefore truncated into a valid record; if the prefix hashes correctly, uninstall deletes the file, deletes the manifest, and exits 0. I reproduced the truncation under Bash 3.2.57. This directly falsifies condition 16’s claim that control bytes are refused. Minimal fix: perform a raw-byte NUL preflight before backup construction or line parsing, as `doctor.sh` now does, and add an uninstall NUL positive control running on Bash 3.2.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:5:- P1 — [scripts/uninstall.sh:424](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:424), [scripts/uninstall.sh:430](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:430), [scripts/uninstall.sh:513](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:513). Manifest-owned paths with unexpected filesystem types fail open. A directory or FIFO reaches `continue` without incrementing any failure counter; a dangling symlink is counted as absent and left behind; a symlink leaf to a regular external file passes `-f` and is read through by Python. The run can then remove the ownership manifest and exit 0 while the managed path remains—or after reading outside the target. This becomes more consequential after upgrade because the manifest now covers adopter-facing `docs/`, `.github/`, and root deliveries. No declared condition covers it. Minimal fix: reject/count every symlink leaf before `-e`/`-f`, reject every existing non-regular type, retain the manifest, return 6, and test dangling, external-target, directory, and FIFO cases.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:7:- P1 — [scripts/uninstall.sh:336](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:336), [scripts/uninstall.sh:399](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:399). Backup and deletion use different manifest grammars. The deletion parser explicitly accepts either one or two spaces after the digest (`  ?`), while backup construction includes only records containing two consecutive spaces. Consequently, a one-space `docs/...` record can be accepted and deleted but omitted from the default recovery tarball. This also contradicts condition 16’s “strict grammar per record” description. Minimal fix: parse once into a sanitized ledger with the canonical exact two-space grammar, then drive both backup and deletion from that ledger.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:9:- P2 — [scripts/uninstall.sh:164](<WT>/scripts/uninstall.sh:164). The new cleanup claims an entire top-level tree after removing any one delivery from it. For example, removing one framework file under `docs/` causes `find docs -type d -empty -delete`, which also deletes unrelated adopter-created empty directories anywhere below `docs/`. Minimal fix: record only the parent chains of files actually removed and apply `rmdir` bottom-up to those exact paths.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:11:- P2 — [templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh:147](<WT>/templates/codex/pre-push-review-gate.sh:147), compared with [templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:221](<WT>/templates/grok/pre-push-review-gate.sh:221). The manually installed Codex gate omits `--root` from `git diff-tree`; canonical files introduced by a repository’s root commit therefore produce no changed paths and bypass review. Condition 26 honestly says the gate is not installer-delivered, so this is follow-up rather than an rc.1 adopter blocker, but it should be added to that condition before the template is promoted. Minimal fix: mirror the Grok implementation’s `--root` and add a root-commit test.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r3/verdict-rc1-3.txt:15:VERDICT: NO-GO — Condition 16 is false as signed, and the uninstaller has undeclared fail-open paths that must be fixed and positively tested before rc.1.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r9/PROVENANCE-rc1.md:12:- parte 3 (doctor.sh + uninstall.sh + templates/** entregues): VERDICT: NO-GO — Condition 61 falsely credits the uninstaller with rejecting duplicate and symlinked manifests, leaving an undeclared P1 deletion path without `--force`. [codex rc=0]
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r10/PROVENANCE-rc1.md:12:- parte 3 (doctor.sh + uninstall.sh + templates/** entregues): VERDICT: NO-GO — Condition 69’s leaf-only manifest cure misses a P1 ancestor-symlink escape affecting both doctor and uninstall. [codex rc=0]
